// A build program chooses by build::os, and names several executables: the first is named
// after the platform, the second `two`, in the order the build program named them.
// The top directory's .ctx files are an executable's, but build.ctx never is.
//
// What `ctxc graph` lists, whole: the executables in order, each with its files.
//# $ ctxc graph . {dir}/gen listed.txt
//# exit: 0
//# [windows] file listed.txt escaped:
//| status	ok
//| exe	windows
//| level	1
//| file	{dir}/one/main.ctx
//| exe	two
//| level	1
//| file	{dir}/main.ctx
//# [macos] file listed.txt escaped:
//| status	ok
//| exe	macos
//| level	1
//| file	{dir}/one/main.ctx
//| exe	two
//| level	1
//| file	{dir}/main.ctx
//# [linux] file listed.txt escaped:
//| status	ok
//| exe	linux
//| level	1
//| file	{dir}/one/main.ctx
//| exe	two
//| level	1
//| file	{dir}/main.ctx
//# remove listed.txt
//# project
//# [windows] $ {windows}
//# [macos] $ {macos}
//# [linux] $ {linux}
//# stdout:
//| one
//# $ {two}
//# stdout:
//| two
